        "id": 40008,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-10-10T14:51:48.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I agree – very awesome</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Vyolynce\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/vyolynce/48/2397_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Vyolynce:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>But what will you do when there isn't room for the foam inserts any more? :\\</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This question looms for me, too, as my lovely briefcase is kinda heavy and though it may have room for one more expansion, won't&nbsp;have room for anything beyond that.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>There is so much cool stuff for the game that it's a challenge to figure out how to store it.&nbsp; This, folks, is what we call a 'Class A' problem.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Kind of related to this, I have found that the original core game is still fantastically awesome for teaching new people the game. What was great a year ago has not stopped being great just because there are better and more things out there. Today, then, when I fly to Houston I will be packing just the original core game. Nice and compact.</p>",
